 "purpose": "The terminal's handle on the separate clock window: starts the tkinter process, sends it the clock state and receives clicks, keys and the window position.",
 "details": "Klokvenster runs `python -m leeravontuur.venster.klokvenster` as a subprocess and talks to it with one JSON object per line over its stdin/stdout. A reader thread (_lees) puts messages from the window in a queue that Scherm.toets drains through volgende(), so clicks and keys in the window act as if they happened in the terminal. If anything fails (no tkinter, no display, process dies) the object records `kapot` and toon() returns False, after which the terminal draws the clock itself: the child never sees an error. F2 (wissel) lets the child bring the clock into the terminal if the window is not visible. The window position is remembered through the bij_plek callback (stored in the settings by the app).",
 "module_docstring": "Het klokvenster vanuit de terminal: start het tkinter-proces (`venster/klokvenster.py`) en praat ermee.",
